\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Critical Difference (Demsar, 2006) diagram across the five template-agent rows on \texttt  {test\_productivity} (Reflexion$\equiv $ReAct and NativeFC$\equiv $PlanExecute in this heuristic implementation; see degeneracy note). Lower ranks are better. ChainAware is statistically indistinguishable from the strongest baseline at $CD = 0.25$; all agents are significantly better than Plan-Execute and Native FC.}}{7}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cd}{{3}{7}{Critical Difference (Demsar, 2006) diagram across the five template-agent rows on \texttt {test\_productivity} (Reflexion$\equiv $ReAct and NativeFC$\equiv $PlanExecute in this heuristic implementation; see degeneracy note). Lower ranks are better. ChainAware is statistically indistinguishable from the strongest baseline at $CD = 0.25$; all agents are significantly better than Plan-Execute and Native FC}{figure.3}{}}
